From: OpenWrt community <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: nokia xg-040g-md: let the ubi partition fill the chip

The board DTS hardcodes the ubi partition size to 0xffe0000, which assumes
a 256 MiB SPI NAND. A size of 0 makes add_mtd_partitions_of() compute
"master size - offset" instead, so the same bootloader works with any
SPI NAND size the board happens to be fitted with.

--- a/dts/upstream/src/arm64/airoha/an7581-nokia-xg-040g-md.dts
+++ b/dts/upstream/src/arm64/airoha/an7581-nokia-xg-040g-md.dts
@@ -85,7 +85,8 @@
 
 		partition@20000 {
 			label = "ubi";
-			reg = <0x20000 0xffe0000>;
+			/* size 0: extend up to the end of the flash chip */
+			reg = <0x20000 0x0>;
 		};
 	};
 };
